WEBVTT

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.020
<i>The time is one hundred years ago.</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.320
<i>Jean lost consciousness when he ate hallucinogenic mushrooms,</i>

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.030
<i>and Nadia gave him her first kiss while he was woozy.</i>

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.360
<i>She has been a good girl since that day.</i>

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:44.830
<i>But Nadia got angry when Jean didn't remember their kiss.</i>

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.170
<i>Jean lost his chance for romance.</i>

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:53.800
<i>The peaceful days on the island have passed away.</i>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:58.220
<i>How long will they have to remain there?</i>

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.650
I see now.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.860
Hey, Jean!

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.900
What are we going to eat today?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.490
That's a secret.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.660
What do you mean?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.540
That's...

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.080
Nadia will hear you!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.050
But Nadia will never eat this!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.050
Don't worry!

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.510
I've had a good idea.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.720
It won't work. She'll get angry again.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.560
It's all right.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.980
You'll get in trouble, just when you were getting along so well.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.110
It's perfect this time.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.530
Nadia says she tell it's meat with her tongue, and by its taste.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.570
Yes, that's true.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.740
She believes she's doing the right thing,

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.490
but for us it's just a matter of likes and dislikes.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.580
But what did the emergency ration she loved taste like?

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.540
It tasted like meat!

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.790
Exactly! That means Nadia just doesn't like the texture.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.880
So you mix it up in order to hide the fact there's meat in it.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.220
Yes. I haven't mixed much in yet though.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.140
So, what are you making?

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.180
This!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.720
What's that?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.060
I finish preparing the ingredients with a coating made from nuts.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.100
Then I steam it.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.480
This is Chinese food, but I've never tried it before.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.740
Is it good?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.070
It's the first time I've eaten it too.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.290
You would make a nice wife, Jean.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.290
If I were a girl.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.710
You're too good for Nadia!

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.040
If this succeeds.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.260
What?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.720
They got a little cold.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.970
Do you like it?

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.970
It's delicious!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.100
Really?

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.770
You should have made this earlier.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.060
We should have!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.400
You didn't mix in meat, did you?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.700
Of course not!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.120
What's wrong, Jean?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.750
I feel like I've cheated her somehow.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:42.670
Never mind that! It's okay as long as she doesn't find out.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.890
But I feel guilty.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:50.100
Nice guys never worry about their past.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.600
Take courage, Jean!

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.560
Who told you that?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.110
Ms. Grandis, of course.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.900
Say, are you planning to marry Nadia?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.570
I don't know.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.700
Marriage? That sounds like a good idea.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.540
Yes, I want to get married soon.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.040
Of course! It's a girl's dream come true!

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.870
You're right. I want to get married before I'm twenty-nine.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:21.340
I want to get married before I'm twenty-six.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.090
I think that, in this age, these things should be done earlier.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.180
For instance, that girl from Le Havre is already married.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.770
But I wonder if we can do that here?

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.680
There's no church or court on this island.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.640
Well, why don't you get engaged at least?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.860
Engaged? You're right. That sounds good.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.770
But I don't have an engagement ring.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.190
Speaking of not having, I'm worried about tonight's dinner.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:47.240
You're right.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.200
We should worry more about dinner than an engagement ring.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.080
You must be a simpleton.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.210
You're right. I must be a simpleton.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.210
Marie wants to go somewhere else soon.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:08.470
You're right. I want to go where there's a church or a court.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.640
Marie wants fish for dinner tonight.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:15.640
You're right. I'm tired of eating squid and octopus.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.520
Squid and octopus?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.980
Octopus?

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.650
Here you are!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.610
What's that?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:26.940
A kite.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.160
A kite?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:34.080
We can fly away from this island on this.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.540
But it's too small for the four of us.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.250
We must start with some reconnaissance.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.000
One of us will get on this, and check out the island.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.510
Who's going to do that?

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.380
That's...

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.320
That's solid.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.780
What happens next?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.240
A check on the wind's speed and direction.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.950
Then an observation of the horizon to measure the distance.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.160
Is King going to do that?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.410
Oh, no!

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:43.440
I forgot King was an animal.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.730
What's that?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.690
Rain clouds!

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.530
My telescope!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.280
King!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.080
The things you make always fall!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.250
Sure, because they feel the Earth's gravity.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.130
Can't you bring them down a better way?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.670
All I think of is how to make them fly.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.340
King! King!
All I think of is how to make them fly.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.260
Really, what a scatterbrain.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:16.180
Oh, no! I hope the lens of the telescope isn't broken.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.850
What if King is hurt?

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:22.350
King can be cured, but a broken lens can't.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.270
You mean the lens is more important than King?

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.110
I didn't mean that at all!

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:28.230
Don't lie.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:32.900
King!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:33.990
The lens!

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.700
King!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.370
You're safe!

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.370
Thank goodness!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.330
What was that?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.790
I meant King.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.260
All right then.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.140
What's that?

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:00.310
Jean, a typhoon is coming!

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:04.020
I see! That's why the strong wind made the kite fall.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:08.520
No! The typhoon is approaching this island!

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.010
Will it be all right, Jean?

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.550
Maybe...

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.510
Maybe?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.470
I've never seen a typhoon before.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.360
I'm scared!

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.780
It's awful.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.870
Is this a typhoon?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.330
Are we really safe?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.540
Yes.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.250
I've reinforced the walls.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.460
I've filled in the crevices.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:17.170
I've doubled the door too. So, don't worry.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:18.800
How about the ceiling?

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.260
The ceiling? With the ceiling, I've...

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.980
Done nothing!

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.100
What?

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:33.400
King!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.940
King! King!

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:54.340
It took us so long to build the hut,

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:59.300
but it couldn't withstand the power of the typhoon.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.090
That's the menace of nature.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.520
Where did King go?

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.440
We've searched for so long.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.240
Let's stop for now. We'll look for him again tomorrow.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:22.740
Yeah...

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:29.210
I'm sorry, Nadia. I should have made the hut stronger!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.960
It's not your fault.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:32.670
But...

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:37.630
You did your best. Don't blame yourself.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.090
Thanks.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.850
We'll build something better next time.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:48.020
I guess so.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.140
Oh, a shooting star!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.650
If you wish on it, it will make your wish come true.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.810
Really?

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.280
What did you wish?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.740
I wished we would find King soon, and...

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:04.700
And?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:08.450
I wished we could get off this island soon.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.450
That's all?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.040
What?

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.000
What is it?

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.920
What's that?

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.970
That mountain is moving?

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.180
No, it's...

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.430
An island!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.870
It wasn't a dream or an illusion!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.330
A mirage?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.710
We don't see mirages this clearly.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.130
Was it driven here by the typhoon?

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.790
Does that happen?

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.250
The theory of continental movement!

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.210
Continental movement?

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.720
Captain Nemo told us about it.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.350
Once there was just one continent on Earth,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.680
and it split apart into the positions they're in now.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.650
But this island appeared here in just one day.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:22.110
Maybe the tectonic movements made the bottom of the sea rise.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.150
Does that really happen?

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:31.990
Yes. The Earth is so mysterious, that it's beyond our imagination.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:36.870
Humans think it's remarkable to see a continent sink into the sea,

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.250
or an island arise in one night.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.960
But it's a trivial thing for the Earth.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.550
Human beings are such small living things.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.390
Yes, the Earth itself is a living thing.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.600
Hey...

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.020
What is it?

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.230
There's King. Over there!

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.070
It's King!

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.040
Delicious!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.870
Thank goodness!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.420
We don't have to worry about food anymore.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:25.710
It seems this island wasn't made in just a few days.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:33.140
King says there's something over there.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:36.390
Over there? Marie, do you...

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.100
You understand what King is saying?

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:41.560
Yeah, because we love each other so much!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.070
But...

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:45.030
I'll check it out.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.900
No, it's too dangerous!

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:49.990
Never mind that!

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.950
We'll be back soon!

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.950
Marie!

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.660
What is it?

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.830
Just now, King was running on two legs.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.670
Yeah, he was.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.220
This island is funny.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.510
Of course it is.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.600
This island was made in one day.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.560
I don't mean that. Look at that tree.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:22.440
The trees over there are a completely different kind.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:28.320
Yeah. They look like coniferous trees that grow in cold areas.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:32.490
And look! I can see something like a desert there.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.450
Yeah, that looks like a sand dune.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:40.410
There must be some secret to this island.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:46.380
What wrong, Nadia? You usually deny everything.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.840
I feel somewhat uneasy. I don't know why.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:55.390
There must be a big secret on this island.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.350
Hey, Jean, let's go back quickly.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.730
Okay! I'll bring Marie and King back.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.810
Hey!

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:07.480
Marie, let's go back.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.740
This island is funny.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:13.200
There's a headman over there!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.450
A headman?

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.210
What's that?

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.590
How awful.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.880
There must be someone on this island.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.300
Human beings?

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.760
In the 16th century, there was a famous explorer named Magellan.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:38.260
While sailing around the world, he was attacked by island natives.

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.430
Does that still happen?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:46.400
That's hard to say, but I'm sure he was killed.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:50.280
Nadia, this island is dangerous. Let's go back quickly.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.030
Yes.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:54.610
But the headman is alive.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.320
What did you say?

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:00.080
Kick!

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.750
Forgive me!

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.420
I'll do whatever you say.
Just please help me!

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.300
It talked!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.380
He's buried alive!

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:17.010
Please, it's all my fault! Forgive me!

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:20.600
It'll be okay. I'm helping you now.

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.350
Thank you.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.980
I'm sorry to trouble you, but do you have some water?

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.190
Water! Water!

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.570
What? Ayerton!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.910
You're still drinking water, Ayerton?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.040
It's very good! A natural taste to it!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.210
You're like a sponge.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:51.670
I haven't eaten or drunk in such a long time.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:58.260
But this spring water contains lots of plankton and microbes.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:02.680
You'll get poisoned if you keep drinking it.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.890
I don't want to hear that.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.520
What I said is true!

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:11.230
I'm an expert when it comes to microbes!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:14.440
What are you doing here?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:19.450
What am I doing, you say?
It's a long and epic story.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:26.830
I, Count Ayerton Grenavan, was asked by the American Navy

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.790
to help sweep the seas clean of the monster. One night...

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.210
I thought you were an oceanographer.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.130
That's the official story.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.930
Even the American Navy doesn't know the truth.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:46.640
Anyway, I found the monster that night, and we began to chase it.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:52.020
I know about that! Nadia and I were on the same ship.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.610
Do you really remember me?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:19:00.240
Of course! Let's see, what was your name again?

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.570
Well...

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.280
It's Jean!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.250
Oh, yes, yes! I remember now!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.960
Jean and Bud!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:09.790
Nadia!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:10.960
I'm Marie!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.960
Oh, yes, Nadia and Marie. I remember you!

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.920
You've really grown, Marie.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.680
Last time I saw you, you were only this big.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.140
Marie doesn't know you.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:28.600
Anyway, we found the monster and attacked at last.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:34.060
We were counterattacked. We were thrown into the sea at that time.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:38.280
So, you don't know what happened after that?

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.030
The natural shape of that monster was...

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:44.280
The world's first submarine of practical use!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:49.290
How do you know that?
It's the top secret of the Navy!

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:53.790
We've seen even greater things, Ayerton.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:56.250
So please tell us the truth.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:01.220
Okay! All right! I'll tell you the real truth.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:06.180
We met that submarine again after you left.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.430
We attacked it in full force.

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.810
Then, the ship shook from a great impact,

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.110
causing me to fall into the sea.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:21.190
I was lucky I didn't die,

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:23.280
but the fleet was gone.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:26.410
I was left clinging to a barrel filled with food.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.620
I drifted day...

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.120
after day...

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.370
after day!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:36.330
Finally, I found myself carried to this island.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.590
That's all?

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:43.760
No, it's not! There's worse stuff to come.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:48.050
Many mysterious things happened on this island.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.520
The sun rose from the west.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.480
The night once lasted for twenty-four hours.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.440
It snowed on the tropical fruit.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:03.360
The sea was frozen after days of dry weather.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.780
Really?

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:10.490
I'm telling the truth! I'm not lying to you!

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:15.710
The law of gravity on this island is somewhat funny too.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:19.210
I found I could run much faster than before.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:23.300
I could jump much higher too.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.720
Not only that...

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.890
There were terrible shapes among the rocks,

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.680
and I could hear someone weeping deep inside a cave.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:34.890
The sea glowed every night. The food disappeared unseen.

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:39.110
Everything on this island is strange!

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:45.110
There must be some secret on this island after all.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:50.030
Hey, Marie is really hungry!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:54.200
It's dangerous here! Let's get back to Lincoln Island quickly!

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:55.500
Wait a minute!

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:00.710
I have more to tell you. This is very important!

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:09.260
The Kings of Terror appeared on this island one month ago.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.600
Kings of Terror?

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:16.060
That's right! That name suits them.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:22.020
One of them was a witch with red hair and a loud voice.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:22.980
A witch?

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:29.910
The second one was a tall, slender devil that had great strength.

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:32.410
Great strength?

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:37.080
The last one was a fat demon!

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:39.210
A fat demon?

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:44.800
The devil also had a servant, which carried them about on four legs.

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:47.760
Devil's servant?

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:51.930
After I was caught by the Kings of Terror,

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:54.310
every day has been a day in hell.

00:22:54.850 --> 00:23:02.770
They forced me to eat food as hot as lava that they also ate.

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:04.900
That's terrible!

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.240
It sounds like hell!

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:15.700
I tried to escape, but was caught and as you saw...

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:21.580
The Kings of Terror might show up again!

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:24.210
Let's get back to our island!

00:23:24.210 --> 00:23:26.170
Yes, let's!

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:28.920
Will you take me with you too?

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:32.430
Yes, but you'll have to row the boat.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:35.100
Of course, I'll do anything!

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:37.350
What?

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:44.810
De...

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:45.320
De... De...

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.190
De... De... De...

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.280
De... De... De... Devil!

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:53.200
The Kings of Terror!
